            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
          %p
          %h2#section_References References
          %p
            An early notion of “homotopical categories” as 1-categories equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            subject to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            (hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            mess than but in the direction of
            = succeed "-structure):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %ul
            %li#Grandis92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the categorical foundations of homological and homotopical algebra
                %strong 33
                2 (1992) 135-175 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=CTGDC_1992__33_2_135_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1992__33_2_135_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Grandis94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical algebra in homotopical categories
                %strong 2
                (1994) 351–406 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00873039"}> doi:10.1007/BF00873039
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion of “homotopical categories” as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+categories"} relative categories
            with the requirement that the weak equivalences satisfy the 2-out-of-6 property:
          %ul
            %li#DwyerHirschhornKanSmith04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"} Philip Hirschhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Limit+Functors+on+Model+Categories+and+Homotopical+Categories"} Homotopy Limit Functors on Model Categories and Homotopical Categories
              %strong 113
              AMS (2004) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-113-s"}> ISBN: 978-1-4704-1340-8
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dodo.pdmi.ras.ru/~topology/books/dhks.pdf"} pdf
          %p Authors following this terminology:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Szumiło14"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+Szumi%C5%82o"}> Karol Szumiło
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two Models for the Homotopy Theory of Cocomplete Homotopy Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.0303"} arXiv:1411.0303
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://hdl.handle.net/20.500.11811/6136"} hdl:20.500.11811/6136
            %li#Hekking17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeroen+Hekking"}> Jeroen Hekking
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Segal Objects in Homotopical Categories &amp; K-theory of Proto-exact Categories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.universiteitleiden.nl/binaries/content/assets/science/mi/scripties/master/hekking_master.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical inverse diagrams in categories with attributes
                %strong 225
                4 (2021) 106563 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2020.106563"}> doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2020.106563
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On the other hand, “homotopical categories” is used as synonymous with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"}> category with weak equivalences
            ” in:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Szumiło19"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+Szumi%C5%82o"}> Karol Szumiło
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://hott.github.io/HoTT-2019/conf-slides/Szumilo.pdf#page=10"} slide 10
              of:
              %em Internal Languages of Higher Categories
              (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://hott.github.io/HoTT-2019/conf-slides/Szumilo.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Usage of “homotopical categories” understood with more relaxed or unspecified axioms on the weak equivalences but focusing on examples which are homotopical in the
            %a{:href => "#DwyerHirschhornKanSmith04"} above
            sense:
          %ul
            %li#Bergner14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julie Bergner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to homotopical categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtube.com/watch?v=OgbaZHpUeD0"} YT
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtube.com/watch?v=SKZT7x_0i_Y"} YT
            %li#Riehl19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                %em Homotopical categories: from model categories to (∞,1)-categories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.00886"}> arXiv:1904.00886
                \&amp;rbrack; in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+J.+Blumberg"} Andrew J. Blumberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teena+Gerhardt"} Teena Gerhardt
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+A.+Hill"} Michael A. Hill
                (eds,)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+categories+and+structured+ring+spectra"} Stable categories and structured ring spectra
          %p
            Usage of “homotopical categories” as, apparently, synonymous with
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+categories"} relative categories
          %ul
            %li#Arndt15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Arndt"}> Peter Arndt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopical categories of logics
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Road to Universal Logic
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-duesseldorf.de/~arndt/research/HomotopicalCategoriesOfLogics.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-10193-4_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-10193-4_2
          %p see also:
          %ul
            %li#Bergner19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julie Bergner
                , MAA review (2019) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.maa.org/press/maa-reviews/higher-categories-and-homotopical-algebra"}> web
                \&amp;rbrack; of:
                = succeed "\u2018s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Denis-Charles Cisinski
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Categories+and+Homotopical+Algebra"} Higher Categories and Homotopical Algebra
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “the two subjects &amp;lbrack;
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  and
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
